    "biography": {
      "concept": "Nine-year-old proprietor of Stillwater's lemonade stand on Main Street (Act 2)",
      "notes": "Bucky Sorrel is nine, wears a paper hat, and runs the lemonade stand on Stillwater's Main Street, which is, by his own account, the EXCLUSIVE PARADE ROUTE CONCESSION. Five cents. No refunds. He takes whatever you've got ('this is a button,' he says of a mark, not unkindly), gives change in buttons, and keeps a one-page ledger. He is ferociously polite, a tycoon. The lemonade is the best thing anyone has tasted in a long time. He will tell you the parade has started; can't you hear it?"
    }
